          "title": "You'll want to know: el piropo",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "el piropo — \"the compliment (flirtatious)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mi marido siempre me echa piropos. My husband is always paying me compliments."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Echar un piropo — to pay someone a flirtatious compliment. From a stranger in the street, a piropo is now widely seen as harassment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "piropo comes from Latin pyrōpus \"gold-bronze\", from Greek pyrōpós \"fire-coloured\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short); the name of a red gem became the word for a sparkling compliment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
